Project: Galaxy Merger Angular Momentum & Phase-Space Diagnostics (Section 21)

SUMMARY OF WORK COMPLETED:
Today I implemented and extended Section 21 of a galaxy merger simulation pipeline focused on angular momentum transport, orbital structure, and phase-space evolution in MW–M31 style N-body systems.

The work builds on the existing density and kinematics framework and introduces a full suite of angular momentum diagnostics across time and radius.

KEY IMPLEMENTATIONS:

1. Angular Momentum Computation Framework
- Computed per-particle angular momentum using r × v
- Extracted:
  - Total angular momentum magnitude |j|
  - z-component j_z (disk rotation axis)
  - In-plane component j_perp
- Established decomposition of rotational vs non-planar orbital structure

2. Radial Profiling System
- Implemented mass-weighted binning over radial shells
- Computed:
  - j(r, t)
  - j_z(r, t)
  - j_perp(r, t)
  - Angular momentum dispersion σ_j(r, t)
- Ensured statistical robustness with particle-count thresholds per shell

3. Angular Momentum Transport Diagnostics
- Implemented flux proxy ⟨j v_r⟩ to track angular momentum transport
- Constructed cumulative enclosed angular momentum L(<r, t)
- Derived scalar time series for inner and outer halo angular momentum evolution

4. Orbital Structure Analysis
- Computed circular velocity profile v_c(r)
- Derived orbital circularity:
  ε = j_z / j_c(r)
- Tracked prograde vs retrograde orbital populations over time

5. Phase-Space Diagnostics
- Built 2D (r, j) histograms for phase-space structure
- Computed Shannon entropy S(t) as a measure of mixing
- Estimated mixing length λ_mix from angular momentum autocorrelation

6. Temporal Evolution
- Computed time derivatives:
  - ∂j/∂t (angular momentum transport rate)
  - ∂L/∂t (enclosed angular momentum evolution)
- Quantified global transport intensity over time

